  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n\n    Central idea: We will generate and search over families of structured binary solutions inspired by combinatorial designs and minimal autocorrelation properties.\n    Why this could improve: \n        - Explores fundamentally different solution topologies than local search\n        - Structures computations around the mathematical properties of low-correlation sequences\n        - Addresses the bottleneck of local optimization by introducing broad structural variations\n\n    Key innovation: \n        - Mixed-mode search combining exact constraint satisfaction, smooth convex relaxations, and combinatorial tournament methods\n        - Parametric families parameterized by bandlimited functions with guaranteed low autocorrelation\n        - Dynamic programming on interval decompositions for offline construction\n\n    Bottleneck addressed:\n        - Overcomes local optimum stagnation via structured perturbations\n        - Efficiently explores (0,1)-sys with ball-constrained optimization\n        - Uses spectral methods for faster convergence in high resolution\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n\n    Representation:\n        - Continuous variables with active-set enforcement: x \u2208 [0,1]^d subject to \u2211x_i = n/2\n        - Barycentric combination of sparse basis vectors: x = \u2211_k \u03b1_k v_k with \u2211\u03b1_k=1, \u03b1_k\u22650, \u2211\u03b1_k v_k = n/2\n\n    Objective:\n        - C5 = max_k <x, (1 - x_shifted> dx/N (convolution-based score)\n        - Minimize d/dx C5 + \u03bb\u2225x\u2225\u2082\u00b2 (proximal gradient)\n\n    Constraints:\n        - Feasibility: x = clip(soft-project(Linear + Variable), 0,1) \n        - Enforcement: update_weights(x, \u22c6)\n        - Active-set tracking: maintain essential support\n\n    Key Variables:\n        - Basis modes: V^K  for K=1...K_max\n        - Mixing weights: \u03b8 \u2208 \u211d^K\n        - Regularization path: \u03bb \u2208 [10^{-4}, 0.3]\n        - Active indices: S \u2208 C{n choose w}\n\n    Solving method:\n        - ADMM with randomized coordinate descent for the basis pursuit\n        - Trust-region Newton-CG for convex relaxations\n        - Hybrid genetic fixers for integer constraints\n        - Frank-Wolfe update strategy\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n\n    a) Initialization\n        - n0 = 512 (parent)\n        - Generate basis V via: \n            V^K = (lowpass filter * gaussian window) {'sa': [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]}\n        - Set \u03b8 = uniform over simplex\n        - Primary_point = \u2211\u03b8_k V^K\n        - Enforce \u05e4\u05e8\u05e1\u05d5\u05dd: primary_point \u2190 clip(np.projection(primary_point, active_mask), 0,1)\n\n    b)Mixed-mode search \n        - Phase 1: Truncated SVD on V (k=3 to 9 dimensions)\n        - Phase 2: \u2207-projected conjugate gradient on 3-10 parameters\n        - Phase 3: Relaxation to axis-aligned basis (nearest-neighbor find)\n\n    c)Exact Optimization\n        - Convert to basis pursuit:\n            min_{\u03b8} \u2211_{k\u2208active_mask} \u2225e_{t} - \u2211_k \u03b8_k V^K\u2225\u2082\u00b2/2 + \u03bb|R(\u2211\u03b8_k V^K)| \n            s.t. \u2211_{k}\u03b8_k=1, \u03b8\u22650\n        - Projected stochastic gradient descent with momentum\n        - Early stopping at plateau detection\n\n    d)Validation\n        - Maintain feasible set via: {\n          enforce \u03b8\u22650, enforce \u2211\u03b8=1, clip solution to [0,1]\n          update_active_mask based on \u03b8's sparse structure\n        }\n\n    e)Progression through scales:\n        - Base resolution update: n \u2190 n * ['2','4','8'][min(2, n//100)]\n        - Upsampling when best_score improves at any power-of-2 level\n        - Auto-tuning \u03bb via ACE matching to bounds\n\n4. Search Choices and Useful Variations\n\n    Initial configuration:\n        - Phrase: 'mexican hat wavelet'\n        - n\u039b = 7 (basis modes)\n        - \u03bb_path = [-3.5: 0.7]]:\n        - Mutation: {'gaussian': 0.6, 'sweep':0.4}\n        - Temperature schedule: 1e-3 * (n/512)\n\n    When to escalate variant t:\n        - t \u2208 {0,...,10}\n        - Escalate early when: \n            * No improvement in 30 iterations at base scale\n            * n < 4*n_min\n            * Score ||\u2207(x)|| reduces by <0.1% over 20 iterations\n\n    Core variations:\n        - scale_variation: 'upsample', 'projects', 'basis_expansion' \n        - heuristic_variation: {'sa': conflicts/fitness ratio, 'eho': boundary issues}\n        - additional_heuristics = ['spectral', 'fw', 'diffusion']\n\n5. Computation Budget and Execution\n\n    - Resource allocation: 1 CPU, 1100 sec budget\n    - Stages: warm-up (200s), active-search (800s), verification (100s)\n    - Time checkpoints:\n        * Every 100\u00d7 basis_size iterations, prune redundant basis modes\n        * Every 30\u00d7 total_budget, upsample (3:1 ratio)\n\n    Robustness:\n        - Invalid proposal: reject with fallback to basis projection\n        - numerical_failure \u2192 fallback \u039b=0.2\n        - n<256: recessed until softverification passes\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n\n    - Feasibility checks: \n        all(0 <= x[i] <= 1) \n        abs(sum(x) dx - 1) < 1e-4\n        score = max_k (correlation @ k) * (2/n)\n    - Return contract:\n        h_values = np.clip(np.array(initial_h), 0, 1)\n        n_points = len(h_values)\n        c5_bound = float(score)",
